-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 16: WITHDRAWAL AND DISCONTINUANCE (roc3, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a flat negative ("may not"), a period it fixes
--                in its own words that has run out, an "if" or "where" that is not met, or "means".
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it limits a grant by its own wording (a manner, a
--                complement, a scope), or is silent.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- TIME.  A period is a constant of the core type `Period` named for the section.  Whether an act
-- is in time is decided against the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (PLAN.md 5.1,
-- S-T1): counting the days is Order 3, Rule 3, and no part but roc1 encodes it.
-- "Subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise" (O 3 r 2(1)) is NOT threaded.
-- A rule that says "unless the Court otherwise orders" in its own words takes that as an input.

