§§ `Rule 1 -- withdrawal of notice of intention to contest or not contest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1642 | 1. A party who has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in an action may withdraw the notice at any time with the permission of the Court.
@ref O 16 r 1 (src:1642)
GIVEN `the party has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 1 the party may withdraw the notice of intention to contest or not contest` MEANS
    IF `the party has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action`
    THEN
        IF `the Court has given permission`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the permission of the Court" (the rule grants the withdrawal with permission and does not say what follows without it)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party who has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest" (a scope limit with no "only")

