-- src:1644 | 2. —(1) The claimant in an action begun by originating claim may, without the permission of the Court, discontinue the action, or withdraw any particular claim made by the claimant therein, as against all or any of the defendants at any time not later than 14 days after service of the defence on the claimant or, if there are 2 or more defendants, of the defence last served, by serving a notice in Form 32 to that effect on the defendant concerned. (2) A defendant may, without the permission of the Court — ( a )
@ref O 16 r 2(1) the period (src:1644)
`o 16 r 2(1) the period after service of the defence` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1647 | discontinue a counterclaim, or withdraw any particular claim made by the defendant therein, as against all or any of the parties against whom it is made, at any time not later than 14 days after service on the defendant of a defence to counterclaim or, if the counterclaim is made against 2 or more parties, of the defence to counterclaim last served,
@ref O 16 r 2(2)(b) the period (src:1647)
`o 16 r 2(2)(b) the period after service of the defence to counterclaim` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1649 | (3) Where there are 2 or more defendants to an action not all of whom serve a defence on the claimant, and the period fixed under these Rules for service by any of those defendants of his or her defence expires after the latest date on which any other defendant serves his or her defence, paragraph (1) has effect as if the reference therein to the service of the defence last served were a reference to the expiration of that period.
@ref O 16 r 2(3) (src:1649)
GIVEN `the date the defence last served was served` IS A DATE
      `there are 2 or more defendants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not all the defendants serve a defence on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the period fixed under these Rules for service of a defence by a defendant who has not served one expires` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 16 r 2(3) the date from which the 14 days run for the action` MEANS
    IF `there are 2 or more defendants` AND `not all the defendants serve a defence on the claimant`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the period fixed under these Rules for service of a defence by a defendant who has not served one expires`
        WHEN JUST expiry THEN
            IF expiry GREATER THAN `the date the defence last served was served`
            THEN expiry
            ELSE `the date the defence last served was served`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the defence last served was served`
    ELSE `the date the defence last served was served`

-- src:1650 | (4) Paragraph (3) applies in relation to a counterclaim as it applies in relation to an action with the substitution of references to a defence, to the claimant and to paragraph (1), with references to a defence to counterclaim, to the defendant and to paragraph (2), respectively.
@ref O 16 r 2(4) (src:1650)
GIVEN `the date the defence to counterclaim last served was served` IS A DATE
      `the counterclaim is made against 2 or more parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not all those parties serve a defence to counterclaim on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the period fixed under these Rules for service of a defence to counterclaim by a party who has not served one expires` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 16 r 2(4) the date from which the 14 days run for the counterclaim` MEANS
    `o 16 r 2(3) the date from which the 14 days run for the action`
        `the date the defence to counterclaim last served was served`
        `the counterclaim is made against 2 or more parties`
        `not all those parties serve a defence to counterclaim on the defendant`
        `the date the period fixed under these Rules for service of a defence to counterclaim by a party who has not served one expires`

