-- src:1652 | (6) An action begun by originating claim is deemed to have been discontinued against a defendant if a memorandum of service in Form 12 is not filed in respect of the service of the originating claim on that defendant within 12 months after the validity of the originating claim for the purpose of service has expired, and, within that time — ( a )
-- src:1653 | a notice of intention to contest or not contest has not been filed in the action by that defendant; and
-- src:1654 | ( b )
-- src:1655 | judgment has not been obtained in the action against that defendant in respect of the whole or any part of the relief claimed against that defendant in the action.
@ref O 16 r 2(6) (src:1652-1655)
GIVEN `the action was begun by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a memorandum of service in Form 12 was filed in respect of the service of the originating claim on that defendant within the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that defendant filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest within the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment was obtained against that defendant in respect of the whole or any part of the relief within the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 2(6) the action is deemed to have been discontinued against the defendant` MEANS
    -- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` is the last day of the 12 months after the validity of the originating claim for the purpose of service has expired.
    IF NOT `the action was begun by originating claim`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An action begun by originating claim" (a scope limit with no "only")
    ELSE
        IF `the date I am asking about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 12 months after the validity of the originating claim for the purpose of service has expired" (the 12 months have not run out; an "if" that is not yet met)
        ELSE
            IF `a memorandum of service in Form 12 was filed in respect of the service of the originating claim on that defendant within the 12 months`
               OR `that defendant filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest within the 12 months`
               OR `judgment was obtained against that defendant in respect of the whole or any part of the relief within the 12 months`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a memorandum of service in Form 12 is not filed ... and, within that time ... has not been filed ... has not been obtained" (one of the three conditions fails)
            ELSE JUST TRUE

