      `the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 2(7) the action, cause or matter is deemed to have been discontinued` MEANS
    -- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` is the last day of "one year (or such extended period as the Court may allow under paragraph (9))" counted from the last step.
    IF (`o 16 r 2(8) paragraph (7) applies to the action, cause or matter` `the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (8)" with "Paragraph (7) does not apply where the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court"
    ELSE
        IF `the date I am asking about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for more than one year" (the year has not run out; a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
        ELSE
            IF `a party has taken a step or proceeding in the action, cause or matter that appears from the records maintained by the Court within the one year`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no party to an action or a cause or matter has, for more than one year ..., taken any step or proceeding" (a party has)
            ELSE JUST TRUE

