-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- discontinuance with permission`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1661 | 3. —(1) Except as provided by Rule 2, a party may not discontinue an action (whether begun by originating claim or otherwise) or counterclaim, or withdraw any particular claim made by him or her therein, without the permission of the Court, and the Court hearing an application for the grant of such permission may order the action or counterclaim to be discontinued, or any particular claim made therein to be struck out, as against all or any of the parties against whom it is brought or made on such terms as to costs, the bringing of a subsequent action or otherwise as the Court thinks just. (2) An application for the grant of permission under this Rule may be made by summons.
@ref O 16 r 3(1) (src:1661)
GIVEN `Rule 2 provides for the discontinuance or withdrawal without the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 3(1) a party may discontinue the action or counterclaim or withdraw a claim without the permission of the Court` MEANS
    IF `Rule 2 provides for the discontinuance or withdrawal without the permission of the Court`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided by Rule 2" (Rule 2 gives the answer; this paragraph is silent where it applies)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a party may not discontinue an action (whether begun by originating claim or otherwise) or counterclaim, or withdraw any particular claim made by him or her therein, without the permission of the Court"

@ref O 16 r 3(1) the Court's power (src:1661)
GIVEN `an application for the grant of permission has been made and is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 3(1) the Court hearing the application may order the discontinuance or striking out on such terms as it thinks just` MEANS
    IF `an application for the grant of permission has been made and is being heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court hearing an application for the grant of such permission may order" (the power is given to the Court hearing the application)

