§§ `Rule 4 -- effect of discontinuance`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1663 | 4. Subject to any terms imposed by the Court in granting permission under Rule 3, the fact that a party has discontinued or is deemed to have discontinued an action or counterclaim or withdrawn a particular claim made by him or her therein is not a defence to a subsequent action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action.
@ref O 16 r 4 (src:1663)
GIVEN `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent action is for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court imposed terms in granting permission under Rule 3 that bear on the point` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 4 the discontinuance is a defence to a subsequent action for the same cause of action` MEANS
    IF `the Court imposed terms in granting permission under Rule 3 that bear on the point`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to any terms imposed by the Court in granting permission under Rule 3"
    ELSE
        IF `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim`
           AND `the subsequent action is for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a defence to a subsequent action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule speaks of a party who has discontinued or withdrawn and of "a subsequent action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- stay of subsequent action until costs paid`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1665 | 5. Where a party has discontinued or is deemed to have discontinued an action or counterclaim or withdrawn any particular claim made by him or her therein and he or she is liable to pay any other party’s costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned to any other party by the claim withdrawn, then, if before payment of those costs, he or she subsequently brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action, the Court may order the proceedings in that action to be stayed until those costs are paid.
@ref O 16 r 5 (src:1665)
GIVEN `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is liable to pay another party's costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned by the claim withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before payment of those costs the party brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 16 r 5 the Court may order the proceedings in the subsequent action to be stayed until the costs are paid` MEANS
    IF `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim`
       AND `the party is liable to pay another party's costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned by the claim withdrawn`
       AND `before payment of those costs the party brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party has discontinued ... and he or she is liable to pay any other party's costs ..., then, if before payment of those costs, he or she subsequently brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action" ("where" and "if" conditions that are not met)

